%global debug_package %{nil}

Name:           sitepull-cli
Version:        @SITEPULL_VERSION@
Release:        1.fc44
Summary:        Headless website capture CLI using Fedora Chromium headless shell

License:        MIT
URL:            https://github.com/isaiahneal/sitepull
Source0:        %{name}-%{version}.tar.gz
Source1:        sitepull

BuildArch:      x86_64
Requires:       nodejs24 >= 1:24
Requires:       nodejs24-bin >= 1:24
Requires:       chromium-headless
Requires:       ca-certificates
Requires:       google-noto-sans-vf-fonts
Requires:       google-noto-color-emoji-fonts

%description
Sitepull captures browser-delivered websites into inspectable local artifacts.
This Fedora package provides the headless command-line interface and uses
Fedora's system Chromium headless shell with the browser sandbox enabled.

%prep
%setup -q

%build

%install
mkdir -p %{buildroot}/usr/lib/sitepull-cli
cp -a deployment/. %{buildroot}/usr/lib/sitepull-cli/
install -Dpm0755 %{SOURCE1} %{buildroot}/usr/bin/sitepull

%files
/usr/bin/sitepull
%license /usr/lib/sitepull-cli/LICENSE
/usr/lib/sitepull-cli/dist
/usr/lib/sitepull-cli/node_modules
/usr/lib/sitepull-cli/package.json
/usr/lib/sitepull-cli/pnpm-lock.yaml
/usr/lib/sitepull-cli/pnpm-workspace.yaml

%changelog
* Mon Aug 31 2026 Isaiah Neal <70036686+isaiahneal@users.noreply.github.com> - @SITEPULL_VERSION@-1.fc44
- Package the Fedora 44 headless CLI with the system Chromium headless shell.
